From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Kristof Imeri <kristof@lanth.me>
Date: Mon, 19 Oct 2026 08:39:38 +0200
Subject: [PATCH 48/52] backends: keep sandboxed apps from recording,
 controlling and rearranging the screen

The RemoteDesktop, ScreenCast and InputCapture services accepted
CreateSession from anyone on the session bus. The shell's connection
owns names Flatpak apps are commonly allowed to talk to, such as
org.gnome.ScreenSaver, so a sandboxed app could reach these services
through one of those names and record the screen or control the
computer without asking.

Only the desktop portal backend and Kestrel's screencast service, the
two callers that ask the user first, may create sessions now. A Flatpak
whose app ID falls under com.lantharos.Kestrel could own the screencast
service's name, so that name only counts when the caller also runs
outside a sandbox, judged from the process that owns the calling
connection the same way Wayland clients are.

DisplayConfig methods and property writes that change displays, such as
ApplyMonitorsConfig, SetBacklight and PowerSaveMode, refuse sandboxed
callers. Property writes bypass method authorization, so a skeleton
subclass checks them before the generated setter runs.
---
